he service behind it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Requests are counted against the credential rather than the connection, over a fixed window of 60 seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Requests are counted against the credential rather than the connection, over a fixed window of 60 seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The start of the fixed window is not disclosed by the gateway.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"whose start the gateway doesn't disclose\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The count follows the credential wherever the caller happens to put it, including across hosts.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"The count follows the credential wherever the caller happens to put it, including across hosts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller spread over many worker processes is throttled at the same point a single process would have been.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"A caller spread over many worker processes is throttled at the same point a single process would have been\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that needs more than that is almost always doing batch work under an interactive credential.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"a caller that needs more than that is almost always doing batch work under an interactive credential\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Callers that retry immediately are most of the reason the cap is there.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Callers that retry immediately are most of the reason the cap is there\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The header is called Retry-After.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"The header is called Retry-After\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Its value is a whole number of seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": 